        >>> data['b']
        array([1, 2])
        >>> data.close()

        Mem-map the stored array, and then access the second row
        directly from disk:

        >>> X = np.load('/tmp/123.npy', mmap_mode='r')
        >>> X[1, :]
        memmap([4, 5, 6])

